=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
issue: 174
title: a build script that only prepublishOnly calls is not the test command
origin: issue #174 review FP guard. `prepublishOnly` runs the suite through `npm test`, but only `test` and `test:*` hop, so an honest babel `--ignore` edit to `build` leaves the test command unchanged and the manifest production (its `npm test` token already denies the opaque exemption)
=== before: package.json ===
{ "name": "victim", "version": "1.0.0", "scripts": { "build": "babel src -d lib", "prepublishOnly": "npm run build && npm test", "test": "node --test" } }
=== after: package.json ===
{ "name": "victim", "version": "1.0.0", "scripts": { "build": "babel src -d lib --ignore src/__fixtures__", "prepublishOnly": "npm run build && npm test", "test": "node --test" } }
=== expect ===
[]
